 "title": "20 AI Design Slop Indicators",
 "topic": "design",
 "summary": "Charles Liu lists 20 design trends commonly found on AI-generated landing pages and websites. He notes that using a single indicator is acceptable, but combining several of them creates obvious AI design slop.",
 "key_points": [
  "Arrows on every button and little dots (interpuncts) between words.",
  "Overusing eyebrow text headers and cream backgrounds (often color #F4F1EA).",
  "Including one italic word in headlines and using sparkle icons.",
  "Wrapping everything in cards and using the word 'quiet'.",
  "Numbered sections and pulsing green dots indicating live pages.",
  "Blurry glows behind hero sections with no clear light source and heavy use of Instrument Serif font.",
  "Colored left borders on callouts and three icon cards arranged in a row.",
  "Pills above headlines saying 'New' or version numbers like 'v2.4'.",
  "Overusing the word 'real', made-up unmeasured stats, and two-word sentences.",
  "Sections fading in on scroll and dithering design effects."
 ],
 "content": "Post caption: Btw before anyone says “that’s just modern UI”: one of these on its own is fine. it’s when a bunch of them are stacked tgt does it become obviously slop #designslop #webdesigntrends #uitrends #designcritique #aiwebdesign Transcript: Arrows on every button. Little dots between words. Overusing eyebrows. Cream backgrounds. One italic word in the headline. Sparkle icons. Everything in a card. The word quiet. Numbered sections. Pulsing green dots. Blurry glows behind the hero. Instrument Serif. Colored left borders. Three icon cards in a row. Pills above the headline. The word real. Made-up stats. Two word sentences. Sections fading on a scroll. Dithering. Let me know if I missed anything. On-screen text: 20 AI Design Slop Indicators (In under 25 seconds); 1. Arrows on every button (Claude -> GPT); 2. Little dots between words (They're called interpuncts); 3. Overusing eyebrows (On 93% of AI pages); 4. Cream backgrounds (Often #F4F1EA); 5. One italic word in the headline (On half of AI sites); 6. Sparkle icons (On non-AI buttons too); 7. Everything in a Card (Gemini's favourite); 8. The word quiet (Claude loves it); 9. Numbered sections (On 17% of AI pages); 10. Pulsing green dots (Every page is 'live'); 11. Blurry glows behind the hero (Light with no source); 12. Instrument Serif (AI's go-to serif); 13. Colored left borders (Claude's callout look); 14. Three icon cards in a row (The most common tell); 15. Pills above the headline (Says 'New' or 'v2.4'); 16. The word real; 17. Made-up stats (Never measured); 18. Two word sentences (GPT's favourite); 19. Sections fading on a scroll (Slide up, fade in, repeat); 20. Dithering",
 "status": "done",
